response:
Yes, this is one way to create bold text in HTML. It’s called the “blink” effect and it’s useful for things like flashing and drawing attention to text, or to underline text. The “blink” effect adds 200% to the font’s size to get the bold effect. Using a different method to create the same effect will produce either a different effect or no effect at all. 

